# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
!pkg/projectmodel/coverage.go
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Vendored dependencies for the offline thin Compose proof's Docker build
# (issue #79 Task 0.3, `mise run thinproof-build`) -- a build-time artifact
# regenerated by `go mod vendor`, never committed.
vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum
!pkg/projectmodel/testdata/**/go.work

# env file (operator copy of .env.example)
.env
.env.local

# Local pilot secrets (PEM/metadata); keep scaffold tracked
secrets/*
!secrets/.gitkeep
!secrets/README.md

# Optional advanced Compose merges (not required; prefer .env)
compose.override.yaml
compose.override.yml

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store

# JS package build outputs (js/semantics)
js/semantics/node_modules/
js/semantics/dist/
js/semantics/dist-test/
js/semantics/bin/
js/semantics/vendor/wasm_exec.js
*.wasm

# Generated output from the thin offline Compose proof (issue #79 Task 0.3)
deploy/compose/thinproof/output/*
!deploy/compose/thinproof/output/.gitkeep

# Per-machine Claude Code overrides. Claude Code loads this file and it can
# override .claude/settings.json, so committing one developer's copy would
# silently change every teammate's hook and permission behavior.
.claude/settings.local.json

# /implement-issue run artifacts: planner output and validation evidence.
# Build-time state, never committed -- and they must stay ignored so they
# cannot perturb the candidate tree digest (`git add -A && git write-tree`).
.claude/.implement-issue/

tmp
